factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 6 problems
  The reel_script says Naveen Kumar was on a Hero Pleasure moped from Karnataka; the article says 'ஹீரோ பிளசர்' which is a moped model, so this is consistent — however the reel_script and caption say he was 'கர்நாடகாவிலிருந்து' while the article says he came from Karnataka state, which matches; no issue there.
  The reel_script states 'அந்தியூர் பகுதியில் கஞ்சா கடத்திய ஒருவர் கைது செய்யப்பட்டார்' and later 'இதேபோல்' linking the moped case and the tablet/syringe case as the same type of event, mixing two separate arrests into one narrative; the tablet/syringe seizure (10 tablets and syringes from Shaik Basith) is described as a sequel to the ganja case, mixing two different facts.
  The reel_script omits that Shaik Basith was arrested for possessing drug tablets and syringes meant for intoxication in the same explicit way as the ganja case; more importantly it says the ganja smuggler was arrested in Anthiyur area while the article places the checkpost at Bargur police station checkpost, so the location attribution of the ganja arrest to 'அந்தியூர் பகுதியில்' is not stated in the article.
  The caption's summary line 'நடவடிக்கை: கஞ்சா, மொபட் பறிமுதல், இருவர் கைது' and the headline 'அந்தியூரில் கஞ்சா கடத்தியவர் கைது' imply the ganja arrest occurred in Anthiyur, which differs from the article's Bargur checkpost location.
  The tamil_headline says 'இளைஞருக்கு சிறை தண்டனை' (prison sentence to the youth), but the article only reports remand to the branch prison after production in court, not a sentence; this misstates the outcome.
  The slides_spec and caption say the ganja was 'மொபட்டுடன் கஞ்சா பறிமுதல்' and the 10 tablets were seized, but the caption says 'இருவர் கைது' while the summary line and reel imply these are the same operation rather than two separate police actions.
